  "notes": "Thresholds are this project's ordinal encoding of published board criteria, not the boards' own numbers: no board publishes numeric levels. They exist so that genre demand and rating permission can be compared arithmetically. Levels are comparable within a system; across systems only through the equivalences table, which carries a confidence value. Boards apply criteria through human deliberation and edge cases regularly surprise, so these values support a conversation with a writer, never a certification claim.",
